              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "SQLite before 3.54.0 contains an authorization bypass vulnerability in lookupName() that invokes the authorizer only for the first joined table's USING column. Attackers able to submit SQL can query a shared USING column in a RIGHT or FULL JOIN to read columns denied via sqlite3_set_authorizer() SQLITE_READ restrictions."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-119377",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-119377\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: libsqlite3-0\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-119377](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-119377)\nSQLite before 3.54.0 contains an authorization bypass vulnerability in lookupName() that invokes the authorizer only for the first joined table's USING column. Attackers able to submit SQL can query a shared USING column in a RIGHT or FULL JOIN to read columns denied via sqlite3_set_authorizer() SQLITE_READ restrictions.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-119377**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|libsqlite3-0||[CVE-2026-119377](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-119377)|\n\nSQLite before 3.54.0 contains an authorization bypass vulnerability in lookupName() that invokes the authorizer only for the first joined table's USING column. Attackers able to submit SQL can query a shared USING column in a RIGHT or FULL JOIN to read columns denied via sqlite3_set_authorizer() SQLITE_READ restrictions."
              },
