                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-97032",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "net/http: net/http/internal/http2: golang: golang.org/x/net/http2: net/http: Denial of Service via concurrent HPACK encoder modification"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "HTTP/2 servers could end up crashing due to inadvertently modifying its HPACK encoder concurrently. This happens because the server modifies the HPACK encoder from two goroutines without synchronization: one uses the encoder to encode a HEADERS frame as part of a response sent to a client and the other modifies the encoder's table size when handling a SETTINGS frame containing SETTINGS_HEADER_TABLE_SIZE that a client sends. A malicious client can repeatedly send a request while changing the header table size to crash the server."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97032",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-97032\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: stdlib\nFixed Version: 1.26.9, 1.27.2\nLink: [CVE-2026-97032](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97032)\nHTTP/2 servers could end up crashing due to inadvertently modifying its HPACK encoder concurrently. This happens because the server modifies the HPACK encoder from two goroutines without synchronization: one uses the encoder to encode a HEADERS frame as part of a response sent to a client and the other modifies the encoder's table size when handling a SETTINGS frame containing SETTINGS_HEADER_TABLE_SIZE that a client sends. A malicious client can repeatedly send a request while changing the header table size to crash the server.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-97032**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|stdlib|1.26.9, 1.27.2|[CVE-2026-97032](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97032)|\n\nHTTP/2 servers could end up crashing due to inadvertently modifying its HPACK encoder concurrently. This happens because the server modifies the HPACK encoder from two goroutines without synchronization: one uses the encoder to encode a HEADERS frame as part of a response sent to a client and the other modifies the encoder's table size when handling a SETTINGS frame containing SETTINGS_HEADER_TABLE_SIZE that a client sends. A malicious client can repeatedly send a request while changing the header table size to crash the server."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-97045",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "golang.org/x/net/html: golang.org/x/net/html: Cross-Site Scripting via improper namespace handling during HTML rendering"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In childTextNodesAreLiteral, walking up the tree previously stopped at the nearest foreign ancestor once an HTML integration point was found. However, that integration point may itself be a descendant of an element that was foster-parented into a foreign namespace (such as \u003cmglyph\u003e or \u003cmalignmark\u003e fostered under \u003cmtext\u003e), causing a parser to resolve the subtree in a different foreign namespace upon re-parsing the rendered output. Continue walking the full ancestor chain and verify that every transition from a non-empty namespace occurs at an HTML integration point before emitting literal text."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97045",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-97045\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: golang.org/x/net\nFixed Version: 0.62.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-97045](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97045)\nIn childTextNodesAreLiteral, walking up the tree previously stopped at the nearest foreign ancestor once an HTML integration point was found. However, that integration point may itself be a descendant of an element that was foster-parented into a foreign namespace (such as \u003cmglyph\u003e or \u003cmalignmark\u003e fostered under \u003cmtext\u003e), causing a parser to resolve the subtree in a different foreign namespace upon re-parsing the rendered output. Continue walking the full ancestor chain and verify that every transition from a non-empty namespace occurs at an HTML integration point before emitting literal text.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-97045**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|golang.org/x/net|0.62.0|[CVE-2026-97045](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97045)|\n\nIn childTextNodesAreLiteral, walking up the tree previously stopped at the nearest foreign ancestor once an HTML integration point was found. However, that integration point may itself be a descendant of an element that was foster-parented into a foreign namespace (such as \u003cmglyph\u003e or \u003cmalignmark\u003e fostered under \u003cmtext\u003e), causing a parser to resolve the subtree in a different foreign namespace upon re-parsing the rendered output. Continue walking the full ancestor chain and verify that every transition from a non-empty namespace occurs at an HTML integration point before emitting literal text."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
