              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-45341\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: stdlib\nFixed Version: 1.22.11, 1.23.5, 1.24.0-rc.2\nLink: [CVE-2024-45341](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-45341)\nA certificate with a URI which has a IPv6 address with a zone ID may incorrectly satisfy a URI name constraint that applies to the certificate chain. Certificates containing URIs are not permitted in the web PKI, so this only affects users of private PKIs which make use of URIs.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-45341**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|stdlib|1.22.11, 1.23.5, 1.24.0-rc.2|[CVE-2024-45341](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-45341)|\n\nA certificate with a URI which has a IPv6 address with a zone ID may incorrectly satisfy a URI name constraint that applies to the certificate chain. Certificates containing URIs are not permitted in the web PKI, so this only affects users of private PKIs which make use of URIs."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-58186",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "golang.org/net/http: Lack of limit when parsing cookies can cause memory exhaustion in net/http"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Despite HTTP headers having a default limit of 1MB, the number of cookies that can be parsed does not have a limit. By sending a lot of very small cookies such as \"a=;\", an attacker can make an HTTP server allocate a large amount of structs, causing large memory consumption."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-58186",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-58186\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: stdlib\nFixed Version: 1.24.8, 1.25.2\nLink: [CVE-2025-58186](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-58186)\nDespite HTTP headers having a default limit of 1MB, the number of cookies that can be parsed does not have a limit. By sending a lot of very small cookies such as \"a=;\", an attacker can make an HTTP server allocate a large amount of structs, causing large memory consumption.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-58186**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|stdlib|1.24.8, 1.25.2|[CVE-2025-58186](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-58186)|\n\nDespite HTTP headers having a default limit of 1MB, the number of cookies that can be parsed does not have a limit. By sending a lot of very small cookies such as \"a=;\", an attacker can make an HTTP server allocate a large amount of structs, causing large memory consumption."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-27139",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "os: FileInfo can escape from a Root in golang os module"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "On Unix platforms, when listing the contents of a directory using File.ReadDir or File.Readdir the returned FileInfo could reference a file outside of the Root in which the File was opened. The impact of this escape is limited to reading metadata provided by lstat from arbitrary locations on the filesystem without permitting reading or writing files outside the root."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-27139",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-27139\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: stdlib\nFixed Version: 1.25.8, 1.26.1\nLink: [CVE-2026-27139](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-27139)\nOn Unix platforms, when listing the contents of a directory using File.ReadDir or File.Readdir the returned FileInfo could reference a file outside of the Root in which the File was opened. The impact of this escape is limited to reading metadata provided by lstat from arbitrary locations on the filesystem without permitting reading or writing files outside the root.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-27139**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|stdlib|1.25.8, 1.26.1|[CVE-2026-27139](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-27139)|\n\nOn Unix platforms, when listing the contents of a directory using File.ReadDir or File.Readdir the returned FileInfo could reference a file outside of the Root in which the File was opened. The impact of this escape is limited to reading metadata provided by lstat from arbitrary locations on the filesystem without permitting reading or writing files outside the root."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
