            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-56857",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "os: golang: golang: Directory traversal via Windows junction handling"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "On Windows, when the target of Root.Mkdir or Root.MkdirAll is a junction pointing to an empty location, the operation can create a directory at the junction target even when that target is located outside the root. This only applies to operations where the last path component is a junction (path/to/junction, but not path/junction/target)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-56857",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-56857\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: stdlib\nFixed Version: 1.26.9, 1.27.2\nLink: [CVE-2026-56857](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-56857)\nOn Windows, when the target of Root.Mkdir or Root.MkdirAll is a junction pointing to an empty location, the operation can create a directory at the junction target even when that target is located outside the root. This only applies to operations where the last path component is a junction (path/to/junction, but not path/junction/target).",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-56857**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|stdlib|1.26.9, 1.27.2|[CVE-2026-56857](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-56857)|\n\nOn Windows, when the target of Root.Mkdir or Root.MkdirAll is a junction pointing to an empty location, the operation can create a directory at the junction target even when that target is located outside the root. This only applies to operations where the last path component is a junction (path/to/junction, but not path/junction/target)."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
