            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-97054",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "For HTTP/1 servers, when MaxBytesReader's limit is exceeded, \"Connecti ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "For HTTP/1 servers, when MaxBytesReader's limit is exceeded, \"Connection: close\" header is automatically set without synchronization, which might race with another header being set explicitly in the server handler. As a result, an HTTP/1 server that utilizes MaxBytesReader or MaxBytesHandler can crash due to runtime panic if its handler reads the request body concurrently with writing the response header."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97054",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-97054\nSeverity: UNKNOWN\nPackage: stdlib\nFixed Version: 1.26.11, 1.27.4\nLink: [CVE-2026-97054](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97054)\nFor HTTP/1 servers, when MaxBytesReader's limit is exceeded, \"Connection: close\" header is automatically set without synchronization, which might race with another header being set explicitly in the server handler. As a result, an HTTP/1 server that utilizes MaxBytesReader or MaxBytesHandler can crash due to runtime panic if its handler reads the request body concurrently with writing the response header.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-97054**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|UNKNOWN|stdlib|1.26.11, 1.27.4|[CVE-2026-97054](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97054)|\n\nFor HTTP/1 servers, when MaxBytesReader's limit is exceeded, \"Connection: close\" header is automatically set without synchronization, which might race with another header being set explicitly in the server handler. As a result, an HTTP/1 server that utilizes MaxBytesReader or MaxBytesHandler can crash due to runtime panic if its handler reads the request body concurrently with writing the response header."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "0.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "UNKNOWN"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
